{"date": "2026-10-08", "title": "Pop Culture Digest — Thursday, October 8, 2026", "link": "https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/", "pubDate": "Thu, 08 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0500", "description": "\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<tr><td style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;margin:0;padding:0;background:#ffffff;border-collapse:collapse;\">\n  <tr><td style=\"background:#111111;padding:24px 18px 20px;color:#ffffff;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#c9a66b;\">Thursday · October 8, 2026</div>\n    <div style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.2;margin-top:8px;font-weight:normal;\">Pop Culture Digest</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:#d0d0d0;margin-top:8px;\">What’s actually dominating today</div>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:18px 18px 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#444;\">Thursday’s conversation: Mia Goth files to end her marriage to Shia LaBeouf, Indian cinema mourns Nana Patekar, Aaron Sorkin’s <em>The Social Reckoning</em> limps toward opening weekend as horror takes over, and Kylie Jenner lands her first real acting role on the same day <em>The Kardashians</em> returns.</td></tr>\n\n  <!-- story 1 -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#be123c;font-weight:600;\">Celebrity</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Mia Goth files for divorce from Shia LaBeouf after nearly 10 years of marriage</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/mia-goth-files-divorce-shia-labeouf-nearly-10-year-marriage-rcna602245\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/img1.jpg\" alt=\"Mia Goth and Shia LaBeouf on a red carpet\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\"></a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 4px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">The petition, filed Tuesday in Los Angeles County Superior Court, says the couple have been separated since July 2025. Goth, 32, is asking for primary legal and physical custody of their 4-year-old daughter, with visitation for LaBeouf, 40, and wants neither side to receive spousal support. The two met while making <em>Nymphomaniac: Vol. II</em> in 2012 and married in 2016. They announced a split in 2018 but never finalized it, and reunited in 2020.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">The timing has people talking: the AP notes that the day before the filing, LaBeouf settled with FKA Twigs for a second time, agreeing to void the NDA from their 2025 settlement so she can speak publicly about her abuse allegations. Representatives for Goth and LaBeouf didn’t immediately comment.</p></td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:0 18px 8px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/mia-goth-files-divorce-shia-labeouf-nearly-10-year-marriage-rcna602245\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_nbcnews.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">NBC News (AP)&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/story/2026-10-07/mia-goth-shia-labeouf-divorce\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_latimes.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Los Angeles Times&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/story/2026-10-06/fka-twigs-shia-labeouf-settle-nda-dispute\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_latimes.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">FKA Twigs settlement&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n  <!-- story 2 -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#374151;font-weight:600;\">In Memoriam</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Nana Patekar, one of Indian cinema’s most intense stars, dies at 75</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cj3vqr5rknpeo\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/img2.jpg\" alt=\"Nana Patekar smiling, wearing glasses and a white scarf\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\"></a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 4px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">The Hindi and Marathi actor died early Thursday after a cardiac arrest at his home in Goa; doctors said 45 minutes of CPR couldn’t revive him. He became a household name as the gangster Anna in <em>Parinda</em> (1989) and won three National Film Awards, for <em>Parinda</em>, <em>Krantiveer</em> and <em>Agni Sakshi</em>, while showing real range in <em>Khamoshi</em>, the comedy <em>Welcome</em> and <em>Rajneeti</em>. His funeral is Thursday evening in Pune with full state honours.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Prime Minister Narendra Modi led the tributes, joined by Akshay Kumar, Rajinikanth, Jr NTR and Riteish Deshmukh, who called it “truly the end of an era.” Patekar was also an outspoken activist who co-founded a farmer-welfare foundation, and in 2018 Tanushree Dutta’s harassment allegations against him helped spark India’s #MeToo movement.</p></td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:0 18px 8px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cj3vqr5rknpeo\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_bbc.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">BBC&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://indianexpress.com/article/entertainment/bollywood/nana-patekars-death-is-end-of-an-era-akshay-kumar-cm-fadnavis-lead-tributes-for-actor-10911761/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_indianexpress.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Indian Express tributes&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n  <!-- story 3 -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0369a1;font-weight:600;\">Movies</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Sorkin’s <em>The Social Reckoning</em> opens Friday to mixed reviews, and <em>Other Mommy</em> is set to win the weekend</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/social-reckoning-box-office-opening-weekend-projections-other-mommy-1236904401/\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/img3.jpg\" alt=\"Jeremy Strong as Mark Zuckerberg in The Social Reckoning\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\"></a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 4px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Aaron Sorkin writes and directs this “companion piece” to <em>The Social Network</em>, with Jeremy Strong as Mark Zuckerberg, Mikey Madison as the Facebook engineer who leaks thousands of internal documents, and Jeremy Allen White as Wall Street Journal reporter Jeff Horwitz. Critics are split: the BBC gives it two stars and calls Strong’s Zuckerberg “dead-eyed,” Time calls it a brisk, old-school journalism thriller, and Variety’s Guy Lodge says it “already feels behind the curve” but is “diverting enough, clever enough and true enough.”</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Variety has it tracking to $7 million to $8 million, far behind the $22 million <em>The Social Network</em> opened to 16 years ago, though it cost a modest $30 million. The weekend should belong to <em>Other Mommy</em>, the James Wan-produced horror film starring Jessica Chastain, which is eyeing $20 million or more from 3,200 theaters on an $18 million budget.</p></td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:0 18px 8px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://variety.com/2026/film/box-office/social-reckoning-box-office-opening-weekend-projections-other-mommy-1236904401/\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_variety.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Variety box office&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/culture/article/20261006-the-social-reckoning-review\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_bbc.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">BBC review&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qIAvWaQJpBo\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_youtube.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Trailer&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_mLfM3L4cLo\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_youtube.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Other Mommy trailer&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n  <!-- story 4 -->\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:24px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7c3aed;font-weight:600;\">TV & Streaming</div>\n    <h2 style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:normal;\">Kylie Jenner lands her first scripted lead as <em>The Kardashians</em> returns with Kourtney taking aim at Jennifer Lawrence</h2>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:12px 0 0;margin:0;\">\n    <a href=\"https://www.timeout.com/usa/news/kylie-jenner-will-star-in-a-bloody-new-hulu-thriller-series-100826\" style=\"text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/img4.jpg\" alt=\"Kylie Jenner on a red carpet\" width=\"600\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;margin:0;padding:0;\"></a>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:14px 18px 4px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Jenner will star in and executive produce Hulu’s <em>Bachelorette Weekend</em>, a murder mystery about a bride found dead in a pool during her bachelorette trip who pieces together what happened while all her closest friends become suspects. Kim Kardashian also executive produces, and Lauren Oliver is adapting an unpublished novel by Flora Collins, according to Deadline. There’s no premiere date yet.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Meanwhile, season 8 of <em>The Kardashians</em> dropped on Hulu overnight, and the premiere has Kourtney unloading on Jennifer Lawrence over last year’s Vanity Fair lie-detector video with Robert Pattinson, in which Lawrence called her “more annoying than ever.” Kourtney’s reply is unprintable here, and she says she told Kris she’d “slap” her.</p></td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:0 18px 8px;\">\n    <p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.8;\">\n      <a href=\"https://www.timeout.com/usa/news/kylie-jenner-will-star-in-a-bloody-new-hulu-thriller-series-100826\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_timeout.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Time Out&nbsp;→</a>\n      &nbsp;&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.dailymail.com/tvshowbiz/article-16192017/Kourtney-Kardashian-Jennifer-Lawrence-Kim-season-premiere.html\" style=\"color:#111;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;\"><img src=\"https://johnmacgaffey.github.io/pop-culture-digest/2026-10-08/images/fav_dailymail.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:inline-block;vertical-align:middle;border:0;margin:0 6px 0 0;width:16px;height:16px;\">Daily Mail recap&nbsp;→</a>\n    </p>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 18px 8px;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#111;font-weight:700;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;padding-top:22px;\">Bottom of the news</div>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:8px 18px 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.65;color:#333;\">\n    <ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:18px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Olivia Rodrigo draws “performative” criticism as women-owned vendors from her Daisy Chain Fields festival say they’re still waiting to be paid; reports suggest it may be resolved.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Early 2027 Grammy predictions frame Album of the Year as “Olivia vs. Olivia,” with Rodrigo and Olivia Dean out front.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\"><em>Ramayana</em> releases its English-language trailer for Ranbir Kapoor and Yash’s mythological epic.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Pitchfork pans Quavo’s Pharrell-produced <em>QRÖMELIFE</em> with a 3.3.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Zara Larsson’s “goon face” hiring joke on <em>Las Culturistas</em> sets off an online argument.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Justin Timberlake jokes about a paparazzi photo that makes it look like he’s kissing a man’s head.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\"><em>Line of Duty</em> creator Jed Mercurio bids to reboot <em>Doctor Who</em>; the BBC’s shortlist is due Friday.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;\">Gaten Matarazzo makes his West End debut as Mark in <em>Rent</em>.</li></ul>\n  </td></tr>\n  <tr><td style=\"padding:28px 18px 36px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#888;border-top:1px solid #eee;\">\n    Pop Culture Digest · curated for John · sent once daily<br>Thursday, October 8, 2026 · from popculture@agentmail.to\n  </td></tr>\n</table>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n"}